# Order Get It Right -- .gitignore
#
# These are runtime artefacts, never source.  They get regenerated
# automatically on first import (or first test run), so it is safe
# for them to be absent from version control.
#
# Closes OPEN_ITEMS A6.  The .pyc cache at
# 02_Technical/src/server/__pycache__/app.cpython-314.pyc that
# prompted the open item is one of the files covered here; with
# this .gitignore in place, no future operator will see it in the
# tree and waste time wondering whether the bytecode is correct.

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Pytest
.pytest_cache/
.pytest_cache

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
env/
